"ai_p_gemini": "Google Gemini",
"ai_intro": "AI tidies the recording into a card behind the open divider. It splits it into items, spots dates and times and fixes misheard words. Without AI, simple rules spot a time after “at 10”, priority after “urgent” and a due date after “tomorrow”. The rules work offline and the note text never leaves the phone.",
"ai_queue": "When Groq uses up its daily limit, refuses (key, model, server) or there is no internet, the no-AI rules structure the note, and in the window after the recording you can tap “Try AI again” later.",
"ai_mode": "Which AI",
"ai_mode_free": "Free",
"ai_mode_free_hint": "Groq is weaker than Claude, but it tidies every recording by itself.",
"ai_mode_claude": "Paid - Claude",
"ai_mode_claude_hint": "Clearly more accurate. Money is spent only when you tap, as nothing is tidied by itself. You set the daily spending limit yourself.",
"ai_claude_only_click": "Claude works only when you tap “More exact - Claude” in the window after a recording. Nothing is sent by itself in the background. The no-AI rules write the cards first.",
"ai_day_usd": "Daily spending limit for paid AI (in $)",
"ai_day_usd_hint": "After this amount Claude gets no more requests today, until tomorrow or until you raise the limit. The limit is checked before every request, so the last one may go slightly over.",
"ai_day_usd_none": "An empty field means no limit. Enter an amount and once it is spent Claude waits until tomorrow.",
"ai_spent_today_of": "Spent today: %1$s of %2$s (about %3$s PLN).",
"ai_spent_today_no_limit": "Spent today: %1$s (about %2$s PLN).",
"ai_rate_nbp": "The NBP rate of %1$s is %2$s PLN per $.",
"ai_rate_rough": "Rough rate: %1$s PLN per $ (no connection to NBP).",
"ai_usage_claude": "Requests today: %1$d, in the last 30 days: %2$d.",
"ai_free": "Free",
"ai_paid": "Paid per use",
"ai_on": "On",
"ai_off": "Off",
"ai_unfold": "Show",
"ai_fold": "Hide",
"ai_p_groq_hint": "The best of the free ones. It is decent and very fast, but misses subtleties. The limit is about 1000 requests a day per model (Nov 2026).",
"ai_p_anthropic_hint": "The most accurate. The recommended Claude Sonnet 5.5 costs about 0.6 US cents per minute of recording (Nov 2026). Opus 5.5 costs twice as much, which is overpaying for sorting notes. The cheaper Haiku is wrong more often.",
"ai_p_openai_hint": "The default gpt-6-luna is cheap, but wrong more often. The key comes from the OpenAI platform.",
"ai_p_gemini_hint": "The default Gemini Flash-Lite is cheap, but wrong more often. Google gives its free plan only to some accounts and projects. The key comes from Google AI Studio.",
"ai_what_title": "What it is",
"ai_privacy_title": "Where your data goes",
"ai_groq_what": "A service that runs open AI models very fast. It splits a note into separate tasks and lists. The free plan needs no payment card, but it has per-minute and per-day request limits.",
"ai_anthropic_what": "Claude AI models by Anthropic. They split a note into separate tasks and lists. They are paid per use, so the account needs credit. With Sonnet 5.5 it is roughly 0.6 US cents per minute of recording (Nov 2026).",
"ai_openai_what": "GPT AI models by OpenAI. They split a note into separate tasks and lists. They are paid per use, so the account needs credit.",
"ai_gemini_what": "Google’s AI model. It splits a note into separate tasks and lists and fixes misheard words. Google gives its free plan only to some accounts and projects. New projects usually work only with billing set up, which is why Gemini is paid here and last on the list. Adults only (18+).",
"ai_groq_privacy": "Only the note text goes to Groq (USA), with no data about you. Under its terms Groq may not use it to train models. By default it stores no requests, but for outages it may keep logs for up to 30 days. This can be turned off in the Groq console (Data Controls, Zero Data Retention).",
"ai_anthropic_privacy": "Only the note text goes to Anthropic (USA), with no recording and no data about you. Under its commercial terms Anthropic does not train models on API data and deletes requests automatically within 30 days. It keeps longer only those flagged as breaking its rules (as of Nov 2026).",
"ai_openai_privacy": "Only the note text goes to OpenAI (USA), with no data about you. API data is not used to train models unless you opt in. OpenAI keeps it for up to 30 days to detect abuse (as of Nov 2026).",
"ai_gemini_privacy": "Only the note text goes to Google, with no recording and no data about you. On the paid plan Google does not use it to improve its products and keeps it for a limited time only to detect abuse. On the free plan (if your project has one), outside the EEA, Switzerland and the UK, Google may use the text and let people read it. Then do not dictate sensitive data (as of Nov 2026).",
"ai_how_key": "How to get a key",
"ai_get_key": "Create a key",
"ai_how_groq_1": "Tap “Create a key” and the Groq console opens. Create an account (e-mail, Google or GitHub).",
"ai_how_groq_2": "In “API Keys” tap “Create API Key”, name it and copy the key. Groq shows it only once.",
"ai_how_groq_3": "Paste the key below and tap “Check connection”. The free plan needs no card.",
"ai_how_anthropic_1": "Tap “Create a key” and the Claude console opens. Create an account.",
"ai_how_anthropic_2": "In “Billing” add credit, as without it the key does not work.",
"ai_how_anthropic_3": "In “API keys” tap “Create Key”, copy the key (shown only once), paste it below and tap “Check connection”.",
"ai_how_openai_1": "Tap “Create a key” and the OpenAI platform opens. Create an account.",
"ai_how_openai_2": "In “Billing” add credit, as without it the key does not work.",
"ai_how_openai_3": "In “API keys” tap “Create new secret key”, copy the key (shown only once), paste it below and tap “Check connection”.",
"ai_how_gemini_1": "Tap “Create a key” and Google AI Studio opens. Sign in with a Google account.",
"ai_how_gemini_2": "On aistudio.google.com/billing set up billing for the project. Without it Gemini works only in projects with a free plan. The “Billing Tier” column shows it, and “Free tier unavailable” means the project works only when paid.",
"ai_how_gemini_3": "Tap “Create API key”, copy the key, paste it below and tap “Check connection”.",
